WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.200
- We have some great big
pieces here at the Bellagio.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.610
- [Narrator] This is Jerry Bolan.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.610
- Here's our water goddess of
spring in the conservatory.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.470
She's 32 feet tall.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.530
- [Narrator] He's the executive
director of horticulture

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:12.900
at the Bellagio.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.510
Jerry takes care of Las
Vegas' secret garden,

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.150
a serene oasis hidden away
from the hustle and bustle

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.410
of the strip.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.793
- These are my plants, and this is my show.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.515
- [Narrator] Jerry doesn't do it alone.

00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:33.180
Ed Libby is the creative
genius behind it all.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.560
- My name is Ed Libby, and
this is the secret garden

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.040
of Las Vegas.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.490
- [Narrator] Five times a
year, Ed designs a new floral

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.670
wonderland for the
Bellagio Conservatory and

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.030
Botanical Gardens.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:44.610
- My career started kind of by accident.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.870
I was a driver in a flower
shop while I was in school

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.620
for set design, and my
career kind of snowballed

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.470
after that.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:53.070
- [Narrator] Thirty-four years
later, as creative director,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:56.085
Ed is churning out elaborate
landscaping masterpieces.

00:00:56.085 --> 00:00:58.550
- I think everything about
the Bellagio is completely

00:00:58.550 --> 00:00:59.493
unique to Vegas.

00:01:00.471 --> 00:01:01.520
I mean, it's completely over the top.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.650
This is not something that
people see in real life.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.259
As people get closer to it,
we call it the up-close magic,

00:01:06.259 --> 00:01:08.620
and they realize that the
flowers are made out of

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:11.410
other flowers and that
the 14-foot birds are made

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.230
out of seeds, and the
beautiful water goddess

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.629
from the sea with a pearl in
her hand is made out of moss.

00:01:16.629 --> 00:01:19.070
- [Narrator] And once
Ed's designs are given the

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.540
green light, Jerry and
his team get to work.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.700
- Morning, Travis!

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.770
- [Narrator] And it's a lot of work.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.010
To bring the floral fantasy to life,

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.581
the gardens are closed to
the public and a team of

00:01:29.581 --> 00:01:32.210
125 transforms the space.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.820
- [Jerry] During one show,
we'll go through about

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.860
80,000 flowers.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.930
- [Narrator] And the flowers
are just the beginning.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.660
There's also 40-foot props.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.117
- Naturally one question
I always get asked:

00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:44.991
how do we get these big
props in the conservatory

00:01:44.991 --> 00:01:47.460
in the middle of the hotel?

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.030
- [Narrator] The larger
installations are brought

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:52.205
in pieces no larger
than 10 feet by 10 feet.

00:01:52.205 --> 00:01:54.750
This is the only way the team can get them

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.600
through the door.

00:01:56.561 --> 00:01:58.990
(upbeat music)

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.440
- We also use a crane.

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.020
- [Narrator] And it's more
than just heavy lifting

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.569
and gardening.

00:02:03.569 --> 00:02:06.150
- We bring in a feng shui
master for Chinese new years.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.330
- [Narrator] All in the name of beauty and

00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.940
cultural accuracy.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.670
- I don't think that anybody
really understands what

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:13.220
it is until they come here.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.630
It's really this incredibly
lush oasis in the middle

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:16.840
of the Las Vegas strip.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.910
- [Narrator] Together,
Ed and Jerry have created

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.860
a uniquely tranquil place
that could only exist

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.000
in Vegas.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.133
Equal parts glamour and zen.

